<article class="env-corollary" id="01KD">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KD">Corollary <span data-tag="01KD">4.6.3.11</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $f_0, f_1: B \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a pair of diagrams indexed by a simplicial set $B$. Let $A$ be a simplicial subset of $B$ satisfying $f_0|_{A} = f_1|_{A}$, and let </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (B \coprod _{A} B) \xrightarrow { (s_0, s_1)} \overline{B} \xrightarrow {\pi } B \]
</div>
<p> be a categorical mapping cylinder of $B$ relative to $A$. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(a)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The diagrams $f_0$ and $f_1$ are isomorphic when regarded as objects of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{Fun}_{A/}(B, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(b)$</dt>
<dd><p>
There exists a diagram $\overline{f}: \overline{B} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ satisfying $f_0 = \overline{f} \circ s_0$ and $f_1 = \overline{f} \circ s_1$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> In particular, condition $(b)$ does not depend on the choice of categorical mapping cylinder. </p>
</article>
